You don't often get email from rsw@rswfire.com<mailto:rsw@rswfire.com>. Lea=
rn why this is important<https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>

Hi, Allison.



I'm writing to inform you that I was unexpectedly dismissed from my volunte=
er position at Honeyman State Park today, one week before my scheduled depa=
rture. I was not given any paperwork or official documentation. I was simpl=
y told to turn over my keys and leave within 24 hours.



I believe this dismissal was not only unprofessional but retaliatory, stemm=
ing from a series of escalating tensions initiated after I submitted a resp=
ectful email expressing concern over a prior interaction with leadership. S=
ince that moment, I=92ve experienced a breakdown in communication, exclusio=
n, and intimidation. Today=92s action felt targeted and final, without proc=
ess or fairness.



Because I had already committed to this volunteer program for the full year=
=97with parks lined up nearly every month=97this sudden dismissal has place=
d me in a logistical and financial crisis. I have no current housing and li=
mited funds until I begin my next assignment.



To help provide a fuller picture, I=92ve recorded a video explaining the se=
quence of events and the emotional and practical weight this situation has =
placed on me. I=92ve also included my documentation.



You can view the video here:

https://youtu.be/B1oe-qvjmMI



I am reaching out not only to request review of how this was handled but to=
 ask whether there is any immediate support the department can offer as I t=
ransition. I believe I=92ve served with integrity and deep commitment to th=
e mission of Oregon State Parks, and I only ask that I be treated with the =
same respect.



Thank you for your time and attention. I am available to speak further if n=
ecessary.



Warm regards,

Robert Samuel White (Host 40423)

458-230-1869



